          DUT's own CLI surface, read with a no-carriage-return `?` probe.
          Objective, as designed and declared: establish whether BFD can be bound
          to RIP on this platform -- so that RIP reacts to a BFD failure
          detection instead of to its own route timeout -- and separate that
          question from the two a careless run grades identically: whether BFD is
          absent or licence-gated here, and whether BFD works here at all. An
          UNSUPPORTED verdict is only honest if the binding is proven absent
          while those other two are DISPROVEN, so this log carries a working BFD
          session beside the refusals.
          7 steps as executed, plus a baseline.
