  => STEP 7 UNSUPPORTED: the gap is not a property of one RIP version. With RIP
     running as v1, `bfd` is still an unrecognized command in RIP's own
     configuration mode, and the identical silent failure produces the identical
     split: BFD detects it in ~1.1 s with "control detection time expired" while
     the RIP route stays in the table with a climbing age. Both versions the
     platform supports behave the same way, so the case is UNSUPPORTED in whole
     and not in part.
